I'm sorry for the inconvenience, but Figma's API currently does not support the ability to apply auto layout properties to frames or components programmatically. The Figma API is primarily read-only and allows you to access, inspect, and duplicate documents, but it does not support making changes to the layout or design of a file.

However, you can use the Figma Node API to access and manipulate the properties of individual frames and components on the canvas. While you cannot directly apply auto layout, you can manually position and size frames relative to one another to create a similar effect.

Here's an example of how you might use the Figma Node API to position frames relative to one another:
```javascript
// Assuming you have already set up a Figma plugin and have access to the current document and selection

// Get the selected frames
const frames = figma.currentPage.selection.filter(node => node.type === 'FRAME');

// Position the frames in a grid-like layout
for (let i = 0; i < frames.length; i++) {
  const frame = frames[i];
  const row = Math.floor(i / 3); // Divide frames into rows of 3
  const col = i % 3; // Determine column position

  // Calculate the x and y positions based on the grid layout
  const x = col * 200; // Assume a 200px spacing between frames
  const y = row * 200;

  // Set the frame's position
  frame.x = x;
  frame.y = y;
}
```
This code positions a selection of frames in a grid-like layout, with a 200px spacing between frames. While this is not the same as applying auto layout, it can help you achieve a similar effect.

